From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: gpu_display: convert half-float RGBA scanouts in the CPU copy

A macOS guest's WindowServer composes into 'RGhA', half-float R, G, B,
A, and its display kext scans that surface out as it is
(VIRTIO_GPU_FORMAT_R16G16B16A16_FLOAT_DROIDVM, DRM_FORMAT_ABGR16161616F
here). The display's GPU blit converts it; the CPU copy into a sink's
8-bit framebuffer had no converter for the format and copied the raw
bytes, so the screen showed false colours, striped, with noise in its
lower half. The copy now converts each pixel as the kext does for its
own boot framebuffer: each channel clamped to [0, 1] and rounded to a
byte through a 16 KiB table indexed by the half float >> 2, alpha
opaque, no transfer function.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
